r signed STORY-260908-18woqo landing; this binding does not accept or alter the preserved partial implementation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nProduction behavior demonstrates: Resolve UUID/name/qualified selectors, ambiguity, list/status summaries, and stable deterministic sorting. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_primary-summary-prefix-clarification.md\n> Pinned bootstrap prefix constraints for future public summary review\n\nPrimary read-only clarification of the partial public-summary bound: pinned SPEC Section5.7 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.md:2277) defines creating as Session Record AND initial lease existing, and Section13.1 step2 (8117) persists initial Lease Record and session.created before process creation. The partial bounds_test.go comment claiming a valid creating session has no owner event is not sufficient evidence that record-only/no-lease projection is a valid public creating state. Distinguish an interrupted persistence prefix from a completed bootstrap prefix; reconcile the accepted projector empty-chain behavior with these exact normative requirements in future scoped review. No accepted CR is invalidated by this note, no replacement state/error invented, and no nullable/placeholder owner or lease fields authorized. Public-summary observation owners and qualified-selector decision remain outstanding; original task scope is unchanged. This is a routing clarification, not tested product repair or acceptance.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-v060.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_resume-v060.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3266`\n- Content digest: `sha256:9bf56cdfdea9340a24a9b8e0ddc69b9772f799f86f29fa469b1433e7c9194045`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-