{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dd5b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a088d5-4507-7282-8481-779aad88dbd7"},"sequence":3336,"recorded_at":1780531400006667,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"12839350-e4ee-4c62-b8d1-5671ff3adc6d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"12839350-e4ee-4c62-b8d1-5671ff3adc6d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"12839350-e4ee-4c62-b8d1-5671ff3adc6d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a088e2-c4dc-7d43-8a99-aa05644702b8"},"task_id":"01a088e2-c4dc-7d43-8a99-aa05644702b8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a088e2-c4dc-7d43-8a99-aa05644702b8","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.6.0, commit\n4|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`, adopted through\n5|STORY-260908-18woqo. Primary scope is Sections 14.7 and 14.7.1 with\n6|shared SelectionPlan construction and revalidation in 14.7.2, refining\n7|Section 2.3 and the authoritative summaries in 5.7/14.7.3. Historical\n8|scope is retained without weakening: v0.5.0 (commit\n9|`28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`), Sections 2.3, 5.1-5.2,\n10|5.7, 14.4. This file records implementation evidence; it changes no\n11|normative ownership and claims no public CLI delivery.\n12|\n13|The v0.6.0 adoption decides the two product questions the partial leaf\n14|left open. The qualified-selector syntax, source-peer versus\n15|winning-owner target, and precedence are now normative text in 14.7.1:\n16|split at the first literal `@`, exact configured alias or host identity\n17|as the source, Section 2.3 tiers for bare input, name-first then UUID\n18|inside one qualified source, and no explicit-source fallback. The\n19|prior stop-line packet on those questions is superseded, not\n20|re-opened. The creating/record-only routing clarification is applied:\n21|creating is a Session Record AND an authoritative initial lease\n22|(5.7/13.1 step 2); a record-only chain is an interrupted persistence\n23|prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf (14.7.4), and list/status\n24|entries refuse it with selector_bootstrap_incomplete instead of\n25|returning an ownerless row.\n26|\n27|## Acceptance rows\n28|\n29|8 of 8 AC rows are driven at the shared-library production entries\n30|named below; 0 of 8 are delivered as a public CLI surface, which is an\n31|explicit caller-integration bound (no `ax` session command exists in\n32|this tree), not a gap in the assigned shared behavior. CLI/Result-5\n33|delivery, wire exit binding, lifecycle effects, and the 14.7.4\n34|recovery flow belong to their owning leaves, which invoke this API at\n35|every required boundary instead of resolving again.\n36|\n37|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n38|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n39|| Bare UUID/name selectors | `Reader.Resolve` → `resolveBare` | `TestResolvePinnedPrecedence`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | Driven: Section 2.3 tiers preserved byte for byte, local-name-before-UUID, `id:` bypasses names for the durable union identity, replicated copies deduplicate on agreeing record digests with a bytewise host tie break. The repository-layer exact-name rule underneath the local tier stays pinned by `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` at the retained `Repository.Resolve` entry in `sessrepo`, not at this call site. |\n40|| Qualified selectors | `Reader.Resolve` → `resolveExplicit` → `locateSource` | `TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex`, `TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack`, `TestResolveQualifiedNameBeforeUUIDInSource`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures` | Driven: first-`@` literal grammar, `local`/`peer:` entire-suffix/`id:` host forms, single-source tiers with name-first then UUID, no fallback in either direction, unknown/disallowed/refusal classes. |\n41|| Ambiguity | `matchName`; `selectIdentity`/`checkRecordAgreement` | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity`, `TestResolveQualifiedAmbiguityAndExclusions`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` | Driven: ASCII-fold collisions refuse within the reached tier and within one qualified source; replicated identical copies stay one identity; disagreeing record digests are integrity failure, never silent first match. Cross-copy agreement carries one narrowing mutant per call site (`N-identity-diverge`, `N-agreement-name`). |\n42|| List summaries | `Reader.List` → `Repository.ListSessions` → `Projector.Project` + `checkSummaryRepresentable` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure`, `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed`, `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult`, `TestSummaryBootstrapRefusals`, `TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole`, `TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse` | Driven: real identity, provider, owner/lease/local role where known, state, newest checkpoint ID, parked reason/retry, bytewise session-ID order. A complete read proving a record without any valid lease refuses the whole list with selector_bootstrap_incomplete, including a mixed healthy/incomplete listing; no partial rows escape and none is silently omitted. |\n43|| Status summaries | `Reader.Status` → `Resolve` → `Projector.Project` + gate; `Reader.AuthoritativeStatus/List` → `authorize` | Same list tests; `TestAuthoritativeStatusHealthy`, `TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeUnknownLocalHostRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeCheckpointRequiresTimestamp`, `TestAuthoritativeInputValidation`, `TestAuthoritativeOptionalObservations`, `TestAuthoritativeUnknownObservationsRefuse`, `TestAuthoritativeMissingCapabilitiesRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeMissingProcessRefusesStatus`, `TestAuthoritativeMissingWorkspaceRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeHostNameBound64` | Driven: named/UUID/qualified/id healthy status; record-only status refuses bootstrap_incomplete. The authoritative layer binds owner, lease, and role from the validated winning Lease Record, owner display names only from validated host metadata (1..64), local roles only with a known local host, checkpoint timestamps only from validated observations, workspace_status from the closed five-value enum, capabilities from validated CapabilitySummary maps (0..7, only available may enable), process liveness as a required boolean for status, and warnings from the projection; unknown required observations refuse selector_observation_unavailable while established absence (workspace absent, empty non-nil capabilities) stays representable. Explicit `InspectLocal` keeps raw access to parked/tombstoned/recovery diagnostics and is not a public summary entry. |\n44|| Stable deterministic sorting | `Reader.read`; `peerCandidates`; `selectIdentity` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` | Driven: bytewise session-ID list order, deterministic bytewise peer-source order with duplicate-allowlist stability, bytewise holder-host tie break for identical copies. Each ordering carries a behavioral mutant (`B-peer-order`, `B-session-order`, `B-tie-break`). |\n45|| SelectionPlan build and revalidate | `Reader.BuildPlan` → `bindPlan`; `Reader.Revalidate` (+ `validateAuthorityUnion` + `collectAuthorityHeads`); `ParsePlan`; `Reader.winningLeaseFor` | `TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts`, `TestBuildPlanPeerSourceFacts`, `TestBuildPlanRecordOnlySessionRefusesBootstrap`, `TestBuildPlanLocalSourceRequiresKnownHost`, `TestBuildPlanValidatesUnionAtBuild`, `TestPlanDigestAndMarshalRoundTrip`, `TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange` (including `changed_nonempty_record_refuses`), `TestRevalidateUnionLeaseDivergenceRefusesStale`, `TestRevalidateUnionTombstoneRefusesStale`, `TestRevalidateUnionAgreeingReplicaStaysCurrent`, `TestRevalidateUnionParkedCopyIgnored`, `TestRevalidateUnionUnreadablePeerRefuses`, `TestRevalidateUnionNameDriftStaysCurrent`, `TestBuildWithLaggingLeaseCopy`, `TestRevalidateReadFailures`, `TestRevalidateMalformedPlans`, `TestActionBoundaryTable`, `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse`, `TestReviewerPlanRequiresLeaseRecord`, `TestRev3RealLeaseRecordIdentity`, `TestRev3DifferentAttestationMustNotAuthorize` | Driven: all sixteen members bound once from validated Lease Records (canonical digest plus epoch, lease ID, and holder from the same winning record, selected by greatest (epoch, lease_id) with predecessor linkage), fixed compare order with per-member stale reasons, revocation class, cross-source integrity class, read/projection failure classes, tamper-evident persistence where digest equality never substitutes for revalidation. The union winner is the greatest tuple across all allowed sources (lagging copies stay current, greater copies are stale); authority heads bind the winning lease digest plus every non-parked source tail, sorted unique. A same-name gain for another UUID never retargets the pinned plan; an agreeing replica never invalidates it. |\n46|| Negative and refusal cases | All gates below | Every `Test*` refusal arm plus the battery | Driven: distinct classes for invalid arguments, invalid configuration, unknown source, disallowed peer, remote read failure, ambiguity, not found, integrity failure, bootstrap incompleteness, unavailable observations, and stale plans, each killed by narrowing. No unsupported capability is advertised (see bounds). |\n47|\n48|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n49|\n50|Every `N-` row is a genuine narrowing mutant: the gate stays present\n51|and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must\n52|reject, and the named behavioral test fails through the delivered\n53|harness. Whole-clause disables are not accepted as narrowing. `B-`\n54|rows reverse deterministic orderings. Controls are reported\n55|separately and never counted as kills.\n56|\n57|| Gate | Real entry test | Narrowing attack (all killed) |\n58|| --- | --- | --- |\n59|| Folded-name ambiguity | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions` | N-collision-pair admits exactly two colliding identities. |\n60|| Exact-name admission | Shared tiers: `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`; retained repository entry: `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` at `Repository.Resolve` in `sessrepo` | N-case-variant admits one non-exact selector at the shared tier and is killed by the sessquery collision test; N-repository-case-variant admits one non-exact query at the retained repository entry and is killed by the sessrepo test at that entry. |\n61|| First-`@` literal split | `TestParseSelectorLiteralGrammar` | N-first-at-split keeps the `@` token and splits at the last one; an alias containing `@` misroutes. |\n62|| `local` source literal | Same | N-local-prefix keeps the token and admits `local`-prefixed sources. |\n63|| `id:` key literal | Same | N-id-case keeps the token and folds the prefix; `ID:` bypasses names. |\n64|| Alias exactness | `TestSelectorConfigurationValidation/alias_casing_is_exact` | N-peer-alias-fold keeps the mapping and folds comparison; `WORK` selects `Work`. |\n65|| `id:` name bypass | `TestResolveQualifiedNameBeforeUUIDInSource` | N-id-through-names routes one explicit `id:` key through the name tier; a UUID-shaped name shadows the identity. |\n66|| No explicit-source fallback | `TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack` | N-explicit-fallback falls back to the bare union on exactly an explicit miss. |\n67|| Unknown source refusal | `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals` | N-unknown-alias-local treats exactly an unknown alias as local. |\n68|| Peer allowlist | `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | N-disallowed-admit reads exactly one disallowed peer; N-unlisted-peer reads one unlisted identity. |\n69|| Duplicate learned index | `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | N-duplicate-peer admits duplicates for one host ID. |\n70|| Duplicate alias mapping | `TestSelectorConfigurationValidation/duplicate_alias_mapping` | N-dup-alias admits duplicate mappings with last-write-wins. |\n71|| Live eligibility | `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed`, `TestResolveExcludesTombstonedButListsIt`, `TestResolveQualifiedAmbiguityAndExclusions` | N-parked-id and N-tombstoned-id admit one excluded identity each. |\n72|| Cross-copy agreement, identity tier | `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` (disagreeing-copies arm) | N-identity-diverge admits exactly the idA record disagreement in `selectIdentity`; other identities still refuse. |\n73|| Cross-copy agreement, name tier | `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` (disagreeing-name-win arm) | N-agreement-name admits exactly the idA record disagreement in `checkRecordAgreement`; other identities still refuse. |\n74|| Read failure propagation | `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures`, `TestRevalidateReadFailures`, `TestRevalidateUnionUnreadablePeerRefuses` | N-read-failure-fallback treats repository-path failure as empty. Missing learned index, nil known index, missing root, and non-directory root are separately driven. |\n75|| Projection failure propagation | `TestListStatusCheckpointAndPropagationFailure`, `TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange/invalid_projection_propagates` | N-projection-failure-fallback omits one identity on failed projection instead of propagating its failure. |\n76|| Plan revocation | `.../revocation_refuses_allowlist` | N-rev-revocation admits exactly the revoked hostA peer; refusal degrades to stale configuration. |\n77|| Plan configuration binding | `.../unrelated_mapping_change_changes_configuration` | N-rev-config admits exactly the ws-alias configuration for hostC; other changes still refuse. |\n78|| Plan source binding | `.../alias_remap_changes_binding` | N-rev-binding admits exactly the ws remap onto hostB; the refusal degrades to stale configuration. |\n79|| Plan index binding | `.../unrelated_session_change_changes_index` | N-rev-index admits exactly an index containing session idB; other changes still refuse. |\n80|| Plan record binding | `.../record_replacement_changes_digest` | N-rev-record admits exactly the parked chain-mismatch record the replacement fixture presents (a replaced record.json against its chain index parks the session with an empty digest); the refusal degrades to the lease reason. |\n81|| Plan lease binding | `.../successor_lease_changes_winner` | N-rev-lease admits exactly the leaseB successor envelope at the plan source; the refusal degrades to the heads reason. |\n82|| Plan heads binding | `.../same_lease_event_changes_heads` | N-rev-heads admits exactly a two-event chain; the refusal degrades to the index reason. |\n83|| Plan absence | `.../deletion_empties_selection` | N-rev-absent-substitute rebinds exactly a deleted selection to its first listed sibling. |\n84|| Union record agreement | `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse` (also `TestBuildPlanValidatesUnionAtBuild`) | N-union-record admits exactly the idB cross-source record disagreement; other contradictions still refuse. |\n85|| Union lease agreement (greatest winner) | `TestRevalidateUnionLeaseDivergenceRefusesStale`, `TestBuildWithLaggingLeaseCopy` | N-union-lease admits exactly the leaseB greater union successor; lagging smaller tuples stay current and other greater tuples still refuse. |\n86|| Union tombstone evidence | `TestRevalidateUnionTombstoneRefusesStale` | N-union-tombstone admits exactly the idB cross-source tombstone; other tombstone evidence still refuses. |\n87|| Plan bootstrap gate | `TestBuildPlanRecordOnlySessionRefusesBootstrap` | N-plan-bootstrap admits exactly record-only idA past the gate; the shape backstop still refuses it with invalid_arguments. |\n88|| Plan source-host gate | `TestBuildPlanLocalSourceRequiresKnownHost` | N-plan-source-host admits exactly idA past the local-host gate; the shape backstop still refuses the empty host with invalid_arguments. |\n89|| Summary bootstrap gate | `TestReviewerBootstrapSummaryMustRefuse`, `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult`, `TestSummaryBootstrapRefusals`, `TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole` | N-summary-bootstrap admits exactly record-only idA into list/status; other interrupted prefixes still refuse. |\n90|| Summary host metadata gate | `TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses` | N-observation-host admits exactly owner hostA without metadata; other missing owners still refuse. |\n91|| Summary workspace gate | `TestAuthoritativeMissingWorkspaceRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeUnknownObservationsRefuse` | N-observation-workspace admits exactly idA without workspace status; other missing workspaces still refuse. |\n92|| Summary capabilities gate | `TestAuthoritativeMissingCapabilitiesRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeUnknownObservationsRefuse` | N-observation-capabilities admits exactly idA without capabilities; other missing capabilities still refuse. An empty non-nil map is established absence and stays representable. |\n93|| Summary process gate | `TestAuthoritativeMissingProcessRefusesStatus` | N-observation-process admits exactly idA without process liveness for status; other missing liveness still refuses. Lists carry process only when supplied. |\n94|| Summary host-name bound | `TestAuthoritativeHostNameBound64`, `TestAuthoritativeInputValidation/long_display_name` | N-host-bound64 admits exactly the 65-character host name; other overlong names still refuse invalid_config. |\n95|| Lease admission gate | `TestReviewerPlanRequiresLeaseRecord`, `TestRev3DifferentAttestationMustNotAuthorize`, `TestRev3RealLeaseRecordIdentity` | N-lease-missing admits exactly idA with no admitted record past the absence gate with a placeholder; the production tests still refuse observation_unavailable. |\n96|| Deterministic order | Order tests above | B-peer-order, B-session-order reverse list orders; B-tie-break reverses the copy tie break. |\n97|\n98|The shipped mutation runner executes the behavioral suites in an\n99|isolated source copy, checks exact replacement count, preserves raw\n100|process exits and named failed tests, then restores and verifies the\n101|copied bytes. It has before/after green controls, a not-applied\n102|control, and a compile-failure control. The latter two prove no\n103|behavioral kill. Measured runs and per-mutant tables are attached on\n104|the task, never hard-coded as a green claim here. No new source-text\n105|gate lacks its token-preserving mutant: the `@`, `local`, `id:`, and\n106|alias-equality tokens each carry one.\n107|\n108|The read and revalidation entries perform no durable writes. The crash\n109|test interrupts the real repository create after record installation,\n110|inspects the parked projection, retries the byte-identical create\n111|through its owner, and observes the healed read. Repeated lists and\n112|revalidations return identical values. This establishes read\n113|idempotency and composition with existing recovery, not a new crash\n114|protocol.\n115|\n116|## Stated bounds (not implementations)\n117|\n118|- `lease_record_id` binds the canonical digest of the validated\n119|  winning `urn:ax:schema:lease` Lease Record for the selected\n120|  session, admitted from `Reader.LeaseRecords` through the\n121|  session-persistence owner (`sessrepo.AttestLeaseRecord` →\n122|  canonicaljson closed shape plus canonical self identity; greatest\n123|  (epoch, lease_id) winner with predecessor linkage selected in\n124|  `sessquery`). The winning triple binds from that same record;\n125|  envelope triples never substitute for it. A session with no\n126|  admitted winning record refuses selector_observation_unavailable;\n127|  a complete read proving no lease refuses\n128|  selector_bootstrap_incomplete instead of binding an empty triple.\n129|- `authority_heads` binds the sorted unique validated lease, event,\n130|  and tombstone heads used for the decision: the winning Lease\n131|  Record digest plus the tail event digest of every allowed source\n132|  holding a non-parked copy of the pinned session. The complete\n133|  authority union (same record, current tombstones, greatest winning\n134|  lease across the local and every allowlisted source) is validated\n135|  at build and at every revalidation; unrelated index changes stay\n136|  conservative stale.\n137|- `source_host_id` is always a bound UUIDv7: a local selection\n138|  without a known local host refuses invalid_config at build time.\n139|- Wire exit binding (CLI Result 5 with Structured Error 1.4.0) belongs\n140|  to its owning leaf; this library keeps refusal classes distinct and\n141|  stable under their normative spellings without registering codes.\n142|- Record-only chains keep the accepted internal projection with empty\n143|  owner/lease facts inside the projector. The list/status summary\n144|  entries refuse them, while explicit local inspection retains raw\n145|  access to the recovery diagnostics. The 14.7.4 recovery flow itself\n146|  belongs to the bootstrap leaf with the accepted projector behavior\n147|  reconciled in its scoped review; this leaf invents neither a state\n148|  nor an error for it.\n149|- Effect authorization (fencing, commit, retry, recovery, remote\n150|  dispatch/admission, transport-resume) and the composed\n151|  invocation-to-plan bindings for attach and logs belong to the CLI\n152|  and lifecycle owners, which invoke `Revalidate` at every boundary in\n153|  `BoundariesFor`. Plans built here authorize read projection only.\n154|- Reads across multiple `Projector.Project` calls are not an atomic\n155|  repository/mesh snapshot; concurrent writers, fresh peer\n156|  acquisition, cross-peer lease union, and differing replicated views\n157|  are not measured. Transports, peer authentication, freshness, mesh\n158|  union, host metadata, and observation contracts remain upstream\n159|  boundaries: configuration, learned indexes, host metadata, and\n160|  observations arrive as trusted caller inputs, and the allowlist proof\n161|  covers filtering, never attestation. The repository/projector own\n162|  record/event admission and validation. No new external provider,\n163|  filesystem durability, terminal, RPC, or CLI capability is attested.","final_result":true}}}
